  n16 d=16   abs_depths=8:280    unit_residues_mod16=1:28,3:42,5:42,7:28,9:28,11:42,13:42,15:28

PROOF TRANSLATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  LRC endpoint x=a/b     -> boundary point of P^1(Q_p)
  extra denominator p^h  -> depth h in the infinity cusp
  raw endpoint debt      -> horosphere population
  BT mass sum p^(-h)     -> normalized frontier measure
  real gap shrink        -> translation toward the cusp

A Bruhat-Tits proof would show that every repaired endpoint core
has positive normalized frontier mass in at least one p-tree.  Then
moving deeper can hide the real gap only by creating more endpoint
frontier, so the pair (Archimedean gap, p-adic debt) cannot both
vanish.

The n=16 rows are the clean single-tree lab: gap*2^h is constant
while BT mass is 17,17,35/2,35/2.  The 35/34 jump is therefore
a frontier-mass jump, not a failure of tree translation.  The n=14
and n=18 rows already live in a product of p-trees, so a final
proof should use an adelic product building rather than one tree.
